# Own-wording Necromancer subclasses of Valda's Spire of Secrets (2024). Shape of tvss_sub_wizard.py.
SUB = {
"Black Rider": {"spab": "INT",
 "f": {
  "Charnel Shield": "When a creature you can see damages you, use your Reaction and spend Charnel Touch points up to half the damage. Reduce the damage by the points spent.",
  "Corpse Cavalry": "**Martial Training.** You gain Martial weapon proficiency and training with Light armor, Medium armor and Shields. **Charnel Strike.** When you take the Attack action, you can use Charnel Touch as a Bonus Action. **Intelligent Armor.** While wearing armor, add your Intelligence modifier to AC instead of Dexterity. **Skeletal Mount.** When you perform your Thralls ritual, you can animate the skeleton of a horse or similar animal as a Warhorse Skeleton. In combat it acts as a controlled mount while you ride it, using the mounted combat rules.",
  "Extra Attack": "You attack twice when you take the Attack action. You can replace one of those attacks with a cantrip that has a casting time of one action. If you ride a controlled mount, you can instead command the mount to use its Reaction to make an attack.",
  "Gruesome Charge": "As a Magic action, give each thrall that is not a controlled mount a spectral steed. Each of those thralls has a Speed of 60 feet for 10 minutes.",
  "Dullahan [Lichdom]": "You become a lich who severed your own head to serve as your spirit jar, so you see without eyes. These benefits add to Lichdom. **Skull Jar.** Your spirit jar is your magically preserved head. Your senses work as normal without it. You see and hear from where the head was, and your voice booms from the neck stump. **Blindsight.** While you carry your skull jar, you have Blindsight to 120 feet. **Damage Resistance.** You and your mount resist Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing damage. **Nightmare.** When you perform your Thralls ritual, you can summon a Nightmare as a thrall. It counts as Undead for your Necromancer features and acts as an independent mount while you ride it."},
 "acts": {"Charnel Shield": "reaction", "Gruesome Charge": "action"},
 "grant": {"f": "Corpse Cavalry", "weapons": [[3, "Martial weapons"]]}},

"Blood Ascendant": {"spab": "INT",
 "f": {
  "Blood Ascendant Spells": "You always have these spells prepared once you reach the listed Necromancer level. Level 3: Charm Person, Enthrall, Sleep, Suggestion. Level 5: Hypnotic Pattern, Vampiric Touch. Level 7: Phantasmal Killer, Mordenkainen's Private Sanctum. Level 9: Dominate Person, Modify Memory.",
  "Charnel Drain": "When Charnel Touch reduces an enemy to 0 Hit Points, you regain Hit Points equal to your Intelligence modifier plus your Necromancer level (minimum 1).",
  "Vampiric Transformation": "As a Magic action, spend 15 Charnel Touch points to become a bat or a cloud of mist. It lasts 1 hour, or until you are Incapacitated or dismiss it with no action. Your gear melds into the form and you cannot use it. **Bat.** You use the Bat stat block but keep your creature type, Hit Points, Hit Point Dice, Intelligence, Wisdom, Charisma, class features, languages and feats. **Mist.** You become a Medium cloud of mist. You cannot speak, handle objects or take actions. You have a 20 foot Fly Speed with hover and can enter other creatures' spaces. You resist Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing damage, are immune to Prone, and have Advantage on Strength, Dexterity and Constitution saves. You slip through narrow openings but treat liquids as solid.",
  "Children of the Night": "When you perform your Thralls ritual, you can summon one or more Wolves, Swarms of Bats or Swarms of Rats. They are your thralls and count as Undead for your Necromancer features.",
  "Nosferatu [Lichdom]": "You become a lich in the manner of a vampire lord. These benefits add to Lichdom. **Coffin Jar.** Your spirit jar is a coffin of grave dirt. If you drop to 0 Hit Points, you reform in it after 1 hour. You stay weakened until you finish a Long Rest in the coffin. While weakened, your Hit Point maximum is 1 and you drop to 0 if you start a turn in sunlight. **Regeneration.** At the start of each of your turns you regain 10 Hit Points, unless you are at 0 Hit Points or in sunlight. **Spider Climb.** You climb difficult surfaces, including ceilings, with no check, and have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. **Vampiric Speed.** Your Speed is doubled."},
 "acts": {"Vampiric Transformation": "action"}},

"Corpse Florist": {"spab": "INT",
 "f": {
  "Corpse Florist Spells": "You always have these spells prepared once you reach the listed Necromancer level. Level 3: Barkskin, False Life, Goodberry, Spike Growth. Level 5: Plant Growth, Speak with Plants. Level 7: Blight, Freedom of Movement. Level 9: Reincarnate, Tree Stride.",
  "Garden of the Grave": "When you perform your Thralls ritual, you can plant corpse flowers in any of your thralls. Each such thrall gains these benefits. **Plant.** It is a Plant instead of Undead, but counts as Undead for your Necromancer features. **Necrosynthesis.** After a Short or Long Rest, it takes root and regains 1d8 plus your Intelligence modifier in Hit Points.",
  "Charnel Entangle": "When Charnel Touch deals 5 or more damage, the target makes a Strength save against your spell save DC. On a failure it is Restrained until the end of your next turn as weeds and brambles grab it.",
  "Rotten Seed": "As a Bonus Action, toss a seed at an enemy you can see within 15 feet. It makes a Dexterity save. On a failure, a seedling burrows into it. At the start of each of its turns, it takes 1d8 Necrotic damage and you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to that damage. The seedling dies after 1 minute, when the target dies, or when you use this feature again. The damage becomes 1d10 at level 11 and 1d12 at level 17.",
  "Death in Bloom": "Once on each of your turns, when a Medium or Small creature affected by your Rotten Seed dies, you can animate its corpse as a Skeleton, Spirit or Zombie under your control. It is one of your thralls and gains the benefit of Garden of the Grave.",
  "Botanical Lich [Lichdom]": "You become a lich whose body blooms with flowers. These benefits add to Lichdom. **Spirit Flowers.** Your spirit jar is a set of thirteen immortal flowers in places that matter to you. Each has its own weakness, set with your GM. If you drop to 0 Hit Points, you reform in the soil at your nearest spirit flower. **Petal Stride.** Flowers sprout in a 30 foot Emanation from you. As a Bonus Action on your turn, you step into a flower and teleport to another flower you can see within 30 feet. You may also teleport any number of friendly Plants within 30 feet to flowers you can see. **Regeneration.** At the start of each of your turns you regain 10 Hit Points, unless you are at 0 Hit Points or in Darkness."},
 "acts": {"Rotten Seed": "bonus"}},

"Crone": {"spab": "INT",
 "f": {
  "Crone Spells": "You always have these spells prepared once you reach the listed Necromancer level. Level 3: Blindness/Deafness, Find Familiar, Tasha's Hideous Laughter, Invisibility. Level 5: Bestow Curse, Fly. Level 7: Polymorph, Soul Effigy. Level 9: Contagion, Seeming.",
  "Charnel Curse": "When Charnel Touch deals 5 or more damage, the target makes a Wisdom save against your spell save DC. On a failure it is cursed and subtracts 1d6 from its D20 Tests. At the end of each of its turns it repeats the save, ending the curse on a success. The curse lasts 1 minute, until you curse another creature with this feature, or until you dismiss it with no action.",
  "Witch's Cauldron": "Spend 10 minutes to brew potions, which can be done during a Short Rest. Each potion costs 10 Charnel Touch points. You can hold a number of potions equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum 1). They stay potent until you finish a Long Rest, then go inert. You can brew Potion of Animal Friendship, Potion of Climbing, Potion of Healing, Potion of Resistance and Potion of Water Breathing.",
  "Nefarious Ruse": "**Conceal Thralls.** As a Magic action, spend 10 Charnel Touch points to make your thralls Invisible until the start of your next turn. It ends early for a thrall that makes an attack roll or deals damage. **Thrall Transposition.** As a Magic action, pick a thrall within 30 feet. You and it teleport, swapping places.",
  "Baba Yaga [Lichdom]": "You become a lich who wields a full coven's power. These benefits add to Lichdom. **Accursed Touch.** When Charnel Touch deals 25 or more damage, the target has Disadvantage on saving throws until the start of your next turn, and your thralls have Advantage on attack rolls against it. **Flying Broom.** As a Magic action, enchant a mundane object such as a broom, cauldron or rug so it flies. While you hold it, you have a Fly Speed of 60 feet unless you wear Medium or Heavy armor. It stays enchanted until you enchant a different object. **Baba Yaga Spells.** You can cast these spells without a slot by spending Charnel Touch points. Bestow Curse 20, Counterspell 20, Contagion 30, Eyebite 35, Fear 20, Mirage Arcane 40, Polymorph 25, Remove Curse 20."},
 "acts": {"Witch's Cauldron": "other", "Nefarious Ruse": "action"}},

"Dead Mist Acolyte": {"spab": "INT",
 "f": {
  "Dead Mist Spells": "You always have these spells prepared once you reach the listed Necromancer level. Level 3: Dead Mist Lash, Fog Cloud, Levitate, Misty Step. Level 5: Dead Fog, Gaseous Form. Level 7: Banishment, Death Ward. Level 9: Antilife Shell, Cloudkill.",
  "Charnel Consumption": "When Charnel Touch deals 5 or more damage, you can lose that many Hit Points instead of spending Charnel Touch points. The Dead Mists drain your soul, so you cannot regain Hit Points from any spell you cast.",
  "Mistborne Regeneration": "As a Magic action, spend 5 or more Charnel Touch points. You regain 1d8 Hit Points for every 5 points spent.",
  "Gaseous Escape": "When you take damage, use your Reaction to cast Gaseous Form on yourself. Its effects apply to the triggering damage. You can end that spell at the start of your turn with no action. Once used, it returns after a Short or Long Rest.",
  "Duskfog": "When you perform your Thralls ritual, you can summon one or more Duskfog. They are your thralls.",
  "Dead Mist Lord [Lichdom]": "Your lichdom is corrupted by the Dead Mists, leaving you a gaseous, incorporeal wraith. These benefits add to Lichdom. **Damage Resistance.** You resist Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing damage. **Gaseous Body.** You can enter other creatures' spaces and pass through holes, narrow openings and cracks, though liquids count as solid. **Fly Speed.** You have a Fly Speed equal to your Speed. You cannot fall and you hover even when Incapacitated or Stunned. **Master of the Mists.** Once on each of your turns, when you deal Necrotic damage to an enemy with Charnel Touch or a Necromancer spell, you regain 2d6 plus your Intelligence modifier in Hit Points, up to the Necrotic damage dealt."},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Gaseous Escape", "lvl": 6, "max": 1, "reset": "short", "tag": "Reaction"}],
 "acts": {"Mistborne Regeneration": "action", "Gaseous Escape": "reaction"}},

"Death Knight": {"spab": "INT",
 "f": {
  "Charnel Resilience": "When Charnel Touch deals Necrotic damage, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to that damage.",
  "Combat Research": "**Martial Training.** You gain Martial weapon proficiency and training with Light armor, Medium armor and Shields. **Charnel Strike.** When you take the Attack action, you can use Charnel Touch as a Bonus Action. **Intelligent Armor.** While wearing armor, add your Intelligence modifier to AC instead of Dexterity. **Somatic Components.** You can perform spell Somatic components with weapons or a Shield in one or both hands.",
  "Extra Attack": "You attack twice when you take the Attack action. You can cast a cantrip with a casting time of one action in place of one of those attacks.",
  "Overcharged Thralls": "When a thrall drops to 0 Hit Points or you release it, you regain expended Charnel Touch points equal to your Necromancer level.",
  "Imperator [Lichdom]": "Your martial skill and necromantic power make you an imperator lich. These benefits add to Lichdom. **Damage Resistance.** You resist Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing damage. **Two Extra Attacks.** You attack three times when you take the Attack action. **Peerless Necrotic Damage.** Necrotic damage from Charnel Touch or a Necromancer spell ignores Resistance and Immunity to Necrotic damage."},
 "grant": {"f": "Combat Research", "weapons": [[3, "Martial weapons"]]}},

"Necrodancer": {"spab": "INT",
 "f": {
  "Footloose": "**Intelligent Footwork.** You gain proficiency in Acrobatics and Performance if you lack it. You add your Intelligence modifier (minimum +1) to checks with those skills. **Weapon Proficiencies.** You gain proficiency with Martial weapons that have the Finesse or Ranged property.",
  "Backup Dancers": "Each thrall can take the Dance action, which lasts until the start of its next turn. While at least one thrall dances, you gain a bonus to AC, damage rolls and D20 Tests that use Dexterity or Charisma, plus the benefits below. The dancer count sets them. 1 dancer: +1, take Disengage as a Bonus Action. 2: +1, take Dash as a Bonus Action. 3: +2, make one Melee weapon attack as a Bonus Action. 4: +2, take two Bonus Actions on your turn as long as both come from this subclass and differ. 5: +3, Evasion (no damage on a successful Dexterity save for half, half on a failure). 6: +3, attack rolls against you have Disadvantage.",
  "Charnel Groove": "When Charnel Touch deals 5 or more damage, the target must dance. It spends all its movement dancing in place until the start of your next turn.",
  "Graveyard Tango": "As a Bonus Action, spend 5 Charnel Touch points to give an ally within 30 feet who can see or hear you the Backup Dancers bonus to AC, damage rolls and Dexterity or Charisma D20 Tests until the start of your next turn.",
  "Disco of the Dead": "When a thrall takes the Dance action, you can send it to the Ethereal Plane until the start of its next turn. There it can affect and be affected only by creatures, objects and effects on that plane. It shows faintly in a blur of disco lights.",
  "Thriller [Lichdom]": "You become an ageless lich with supernatural grace. These benefits add to Lichdom. **Dance-Off.** As a Magic action, spend 20 Charnel Touch points to challenge up to ten creatures you can see within 60 feet. Each makes a Charisma save against your spell save DC, taking 8d6 Psychic damage on a failure or half on a success. **Moonwalk.** You can cast Freedom of Movement on your thralls or yourself without a slot. **Smooth Criminal.** Your Dexterity and Charisma increase by 4, to a maximum of 25."},
 "acts": {"Graveyard Tango": "bonus", "Thriller [Lichdom]": "action"},
 "fx": [[3, "Footloose", {"skills": ["Acrobatics", "Performance"], "notes": [["Note", "Footloose: add Intelligence modifier (min +1) to Acrobatics and Performance checks"]]}]]},

"Overlord": {"spab": "INT",
 "f": {
  "Overlord Spells": "You always have these spells prepared once you reach the listed Necromancer level. Level 3: Bane, Command, Detect Thoughts, Hold Person. Level 5: Haste, Slow. Level 7: Compulsion, Confusion. Level 9: Dominate Person, Geas.",
  "Charnel Aura": "As a Bonus Action, spend 5 or more Charnel Touch points to make a 30 foot Emanation around you until the start of your next turn. Undead you control inside it gain a bonus to D20 Tests, damage rolls and AC. The bonus is +1 per 5 points spent, to a maximum of +3.",
  "Despotic Discourse": "You add your Intelligence modifier (minimum +1) to Charisma checks made with Deception, Intimidation and Persuasion.",
  "Sacrificial Thralls": "When an attack roll hits you, use your Reaction to make it hit one of your thralls within 5 feet instead. Once used, it returns after a Short or Long Rest. You can also restore it by spending a level 2+ spell slot, with no action needed.",
  "Tyrant [Lichdom]": "Your hunger for control makes you a tyrant lich, a hooded husk with two glowing dots for eyes. These benefits add to Lichdom. **Possession.** If you drop to 0 Hit Points, you may possess a body instead of reforming at your spirit jar. Pick a Humanoid or one of your thralls within 120 feet. A Humanoid must succeed on a Charisma save against your spell save DC or be possessed. A creature that succeeds is immune to your Possession for 24 hours. You control the body, though a Humanoid stays aware. Your statistics are replaced by the body's, but you keep your alignment, Intelligence, Wisdom, Charisma, class features and feats. You cannot use class features the target has. A possessed Humanoid repeats the save every 8 hours, ending the Possession on a success and ejecting you. It also ends if the body drops to 0 Hit Points or you end it as a Magic action. **Domination Spells.** You can cast these spells without a slot by spending Charnel Touch points. Command 15, Dominate Beast 20, Dominate Monster 60, Dominate Person 30, Geas 30."},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Sacrificial Thralls", "lvl": 10, "max": 1, "reset": "short", "tag": "Reaction"}],
 "acts": {"Charnel Aura": "bonus", "Sacrificial Thralls": "reaction"}},

"Pale Master": {"spab": "INT",
 "f": {
  "Pale Master Spells": "You always have these spells prepared once you reach the listed Necromancer level. Level 3: Exhume, Invisibility, Might of the Abyss, Ray of Enfeeblement. Level 5: Fear, Speak with Dead. Level 7: Evard's Black Tentacles, Blight. Level 9: Cloudkill, Scrying.",
  "Charnel Empower": "When a level 1+ Necromancy spell deals damage, you can spend Charnel Touch points up to your Necromancer level plus your Intelligence modifier. One target of the spell takes extra Necrotic damage equal to the points spent.",
  "Chilling Disposition": "**Intelligent Intimidation.** You gain Intimidation proficiency if you lack it, and add your Intelligence modifier (minimum +1) to its checks. **Frightening Gaze.** As a Bonus Action, spend 10 Charnel Touch points to fix your gaze on a creature you can see within 60 feet. It makes a Wisdom save against your spell save DC or is Frightened for 1 minute. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the condition on a success.",
  "Thrall Rush": "When you roll Initiative, you can empty your Dead Space, and each thrall can move up to its Speed.",
  "Archlich [Lichdom]": "Your skin tightens on your bones, yet you radiate great power. These benefits add to Lichdom. **Devour Soul.** When you reduce an enemy to 0 Hit Points, you can devour its soul with no action. Roll a d8 and regain expended spell slots of your choice whose combined level is no more than the roll. Once used, it returns after a Long Rest. A creature whose soul is devoured can be restored to life only by Wish. **Magic Resistance.** You have Advantage on saves against spells and other magical effects. **Paralyzing Touch.** When Charnel Touch deals 30 or more damage, the target is Paralyzed until the start of your next turn."},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Archlich [Lichdom]", "n": "Devour Soul", "lvl": 20, "max": 1, "reset": "long", "tag": "Free"}],
 "acts": {"Chilling Disposition": "bonus"},
 "fx": [[6, "Chilling Disposition", {"skills": ["Intimidation"], "notes": [["Note", "Intelligent Intimidation: add Intelligence modifier (min +1) to Intimidation checks"]]}]]},

"Pharaoh": {"spab": "INT",
 "f": {
  "Pharaoh Spells": "You always have these spells prepared once you reach the listed Necromancer level. Level 3: Bless, Darkness, Guiding Bolt, Lesser Restoration, Thaumaturgy. Level 5: Bestow Curse, Revivify. Level 7: Death Ward, Divination. Level 9: Insect Plague, Greater Restoration.",
  "Holy Symbol": "You can use a Holy Symbol as a Spellcasting Focus for your Necromancer spells.",
  "Channel Divinity": "You channel pseudo-divinity into magical effects. You start with Ankh of Radiance and gain more options at higher levels. Each use, choose one effect. You have two uses. A Short Rest returns one and a Long Rest returns all. You can also restore one use by spending 15 Charnel Touch points, with no action needed. **Ankh of Radiance.** As a Magic action, brandish your Holy Symbol and bless up to your Intelligence modifier (minimum 1) allies you can see within 60 feet for 1 minute. The first time a blessed creature takes damage, it resists that damage. If the damage came from a melee attack, the attacker takes 1d6 Radiant damage. Then the blessing ends for that creature. The Radiant damage becomes 2d6 at level 5, 3d6 at level 11 and 4d6 at level 17.",
  "Mock Divinity": "When you cast Thaumaturgy, you can use any number of its effects. You also gain these effects. **Avatar.** At a point within range, manifest a Huge illusory avatar for 1 minute. You set its look. It copies your movements and projects your speech in a booming voice. **Gathering Storm.** Clouds churn overhead for 1 minute. You set their look and whether thunder, lightning or light rain comes with them. **Sun and Moon.** For 1 minute, brighten or darken the sun or moon. Within range, you can change Darkness to Dim Light and Dim Light to Bright Light, or the reverse.",
  "Scarab of Judgment": "Spend a use of Channel Divinity. As a Magic action, touch one of your thralls and pick a willing Humanoid you can see within 60 feet. The Undead turns to dust, and the Humanoid regains Hit Points equal to the Undead's Hit Points. A creature healed this way cannot be healed this way again until it finishes a Long Rest.",
  "Mummy Lord [Lichdom]": "You undergo the funeral rites of the pharaohs and become a mummy lord. These benefits add to Lichdom. **Canopic Jars.** Your spirit jar is four canopic jars holding your stomach, lungs, intestines and liver. Each has a weakness, set with your GM. You are stopped for good only when all four are destroyed. When you are destroyed, you reform at your sarcophagus. **Magic Resistance.** You have Advantage on saves against spells and other magical effects. **Mummy Rot.** When Charnel Touch deals 20 or more damage, the target is cursed. A cursed target cannot regain Hit Points, its Hit Point maximum does not return to normal after a Long Rest, and the maximum drops by 3d6 every 24 hours. A creature reduced to 0 Hit Points by this attack dies and turns to dust. **Whirlwind of Sand.** As a Bonus Action, become a whirlwind of sand, move up to 60 feet, and return to normal. In whirlwind form you are immune to all damage and to the Grappled, Petrified, Prone, Restrained and Stunned conditions. You keep your worn and carried gear."},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Channel Divinity", "n": "Channel Divinity (Pharaoh)", "lvl": 3, "max": 2, "reset": "short1", "tag": "Magic action"}],
 "acts": {"Channel Divinity": "action"}},

"Plague Lord": {"spab": "INT",
 "f": {
  "Charnel Toxin": "When Charnel Touch deals 5 or more damage, the target is Poisoned until the start of your next turn.",
  "Necrotoxin": "A Necromancer spell or feature of yours that deals Poison damage or inflicts the Poisoned condition ignores Resistance to Poison damage and Immunity to the Poisoned condition.",
  "Vile Congregation": "Vermin cling to you and swarm those near you. When an enemy within 5 feet of you makes a D20 Test, you can subtract 1d4 from the roll.",
  "Projectile Spew": "Your reach with Charnel Touch and with spells that have a range of Touch is 10 feet greater than normal.",
  "Bloated Thralls": "When a thrall drops to 0 Hit Points or you release it, it can burst in toxic gore. Each creature you choose within 5 feet of it makes a Dexterity save against your spell save DC. On a failure, a creature takes 4d6 Poison damage and is Poisoned until the start of your next turn. On a success, it takes half damage.",
  "Corpulent Lich [Lichdom]": "Your love of rot bloats you like a waterlogged corpse. These benefits add to Lichdom. **Gore Burst.** When you drop to 0 Hit Points, your body bursts. Each creature you choose within 20 feet makes a Dexterity save against your spell save DC. On a failure, it takes 5d10 Poison and 5d10 Necrotic damage and is Poisoned until the start of your next turn. On a success, it takes half damage. **Master of Disease.** When Charnel Touch deals 25 or more damage, the target is Poisoned and cursed for 1 minute. Choose two effects below to afflict it while cursed. At the end of each of its turns it makes a Constitution save against your spell save DC, ending the curse and the Poisoned condition on a success. Bleeding: each time it takes damage, it takes an extra 1d6 Necrotic damage. Disadvantage: pick one ability, and the target has Disadvantage on checks and saves with it. Garbled: it cannot speak coherently or cast spells with a Verbal component. Red-Eye: it is Blinded beyond 10 feet. Unsteady: it is Prone at the end of each of its turns."}},

"Reanimator": {"spab": "INT",
 "f": {
  "Charnel Voltage": "When Charnel Touch deals 5 or more damage, you can make it Lightning damage and arc to a second creature within 5 feet of the target. That creature makes a Dexterity save against your spell save DC. On a failure it takes Lightning damage equal to half the Charnel Touch points spent. A creature that takes this damage cannot make Opportunity Attacks until the start of its next turn.",
  "Skilled Surgeon": "You gain Medicine proficiency if you lack it, and add your Intelligence modifier (minimum +1) to Medicine checks.",
  "Spell-Stitching": "Over 1 hour, which can be done during a Short or Long Rest, spend Charnel Touch points to sew Spell-Stitches into your thralls. The cost is in parentheses. Each thrall holds up to two stitches. They last until the thrall dies or you replace one. **Armored Stitch (15).** The thrall's AC becomes 18 if it was lower. **Fleet Stitch (5).** The thrall's Speed is doubled. **Skilled Stitch (5).** The thrall has proficiency in all your skills. **Tough Stitch (10).** The thrall's Hit Point maximum and current Hit Points increase by twice your Necromancer level. **Vicious Stitch (10).** The thrall has Advantage on the first attack roll of each of its turns.",
  "Lazarus Bolt": "As a Magic action, drive a bolt into the torso of a creature within 5 feet that died within the last minute. It revives with 1 Hit Point and gains Temporary Hit Points equal to twice your Necromancer level. It fails on a creature with no heart, one that died of old age, or one missing vital organs. Once used, it returns after a Long Rest. You can also restore it by spending 20 Charnel Touch points, with no action needed.",
  "Quick Stitch": "As a Magic action, apply a Spell-Stitch to a thrall, spending Charnel Touch points as normal. It lasts 10 minutes and can exceed the thrall's limit of two stitches.",
  "Patchwork Golem [Lichdom]": "You build an artificial body as a vessel for your soul. These benefits add to Lichdom. **Golem Body.** Your spirit jar is your golem body, which has a weakness set with your GM. You are stopped for good only if the body is destroyed using that weakness. If you drop to 0 Hit Points, you die for a time and reanimate with half your Hit Points after 1 hour. **Gruesome Physicality.** Your Strength, Dexterity and Constitution become 20 if they were lower. **Damage Resistance.** You resist Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing damage. **Self-Stitches.** As a Magic action, apply any number of Spell-Stitches to yourself, spending Charnel Touch points as normal. They last until you finish a Long Rest."},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Lazarus Bolt", "lvl": 6, "max": 1, "reset": "long", "tag": "Magic action"}],
 "acts": {"Lazarus Bolt": "action", "Quick Stitch": "action"},
 "fx": [[3, "Skilled Surgeon", {"skills": ["Medicine"], "notes": [["Note", "Skilled Surgeon: add Intelligence modifier (min +1) to Medicine checks"]]}]]},

"Reaper": {"spab": "INT",
 "f": {
  "Reaper Spells": "You always have these spells prepared once you reach the listed Necromancer level. Level 3: False Life, Inflict Wounds, Invisibility, Silence. Level 5: Fear, Speak with Dead. Level 7: Greater Invisibility, Phantasmal Killer. Level 9: Mislead, Passwall.",
  "Charnel Veil": "When Charnel Touch deals 5 or more damage, you become Invisible until the start of your next turn.",
  "Umbral Form": "As a Magic action, flatten into a shadow on the floor. You stay in it until you leave as a Bonus Action. **Inactive.** You cannot take actions, Bonus Actions or Reactions, except to leave the form. **Immunities.** You are immune to Grappled and Prone. **Difficult Target.** Attacks against you have Disadvantage. **Invisible in Darkness.** While entirely in Darkness, you are Invisible to any creature that relies on Darkvision to see you there. **Speed.** Your Speed doubles and you gain a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. You cross difficult surfaces, ceilings included, with no check. You can only move along surfaces and cannot jump or fly. **Gear.** Your equipment merges with the form and does nothing until you leave it.",
  "Wraith Flight": "Each thrall gains a Fly Speed equal to its Speed. A thrall that already flies has its Fly Speed doubled. Flying thralls do not provoke Opportunity Attacks.",
  "Harbinger [Lichdom]": "You become death itself, a skeletal figure in a dark robe. These benefits add to Lichdom. **Death's Touch.** When you use Charnel Touch and roll 11 or higher on the d20, you hit regardless of the target's AC. **Fell Flight.** You have a Fly Speed of 60 feet. **Grim Harvest.** When Charnel Touch kills a Medium or Small creature that is not Undead, you rip out its soul. It animates as a Specter under your control and counts as one of your thralls."},
 "acts": {"Umbral Form": "action"}},

"Toymaker": {"spab": "INT",
 "f": {
  "Slaymates": "You bind the souls of the dead into Construct vessels such as porcelain dolls, clockwork toys, wooden puppets and stuffed animals. When you perform your Thralls ritual, you can create one or more Slaymates. They are your thralls and count as Undead for your Necromancer features. Two Slaymates count as one thrall for your thrall limit and for the Undead stored in your Dead Space.",
  "Charnel Puppet": "As a Magic action, spend 5 or more Charnel Touch points to animate two Slaymates under your control for every 5 points spent. They count as your thralls and appear in your space or an open space within 5 feet.",
  "Soul Doll": "When a creature you can see within 60 feet dies, use your Reaction to trap its soul in a Soul Doll. The creature controls the doll using the Slaymate stat block, but cannot attack. It keeps its alignment, personality, languages, Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma. You do not control it and it is not one of your thralls. It need not cooperate, especially if you act against it or it sees you as an enemy. While trapped, the soul cannot return to life. The soul leaves when the doll is reduced to 0 Hit Points or when you release it as a Magic action. You can have up to five Soul Dolls. When you make a new one, you can release another as part of the same Reaction.",
  "Miniature Minions": "When you perform your Thralls ritual, any thrall you create can be Tiny with a toylike look of your choice. A Tiny thrall has a +3 bonus to AC.",
  "Clockwork Lich [Lichdom]": "You move your soul into a ticking clockwork body. These benefits add to Lichdom. **Clockwork Body.** Your soul is bound to a Construct body with your statistics. Your type is Construct instead of Undead. **Clockwork Immunities.** You are immune to the Blinded, Charmed, Deafened, Frightened, Paralyzed and Stunned conditions. **Spell Immunities.** You are immune to three spells of your choice, picked when you build the body. **Backup Body.** You can spend 10 days and materials worth 1,000+ GP to build another clockwork body as a safeguard. When you die, your soul moves to another clockwork body you built. If none is available, you reform at your spirit jar in a Slaymate body, keeping your alignment, personality, Intelligence, Wisdom, Charisma and the ability to build a clockwork body."},
 "acts": {"Charnel Puppet": "action", "Soul Doll": "reaction"}},
}
